{{also|Stellen|stëllen}}
==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈstɛlə(n)/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-stellen.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|stel|len}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɛlən|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|stellen}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|*stellen}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*stalljan}}.

====Verb====
{{nl-verb}}

# {{lb|nl|transitive}} to [[position]]; place
#: {{ux|nl|Ze '''stelden''' de meubels opnieuw op in de kamer.|They '''positioned''' the furniture again in the room.}}
#: {{ux|nl|De beeldhouwer '''stelde''' zijn standbeeld tentoon in het park.|The sculptor '''placed''' his statue on display in the park.}}
# {{lb|nl|transitive}} to [[state]], to put forward (a question or problem)
#: {{ux|nl|De leraar '''stelde''' een moeilijke vraag.|The teacher '''stated''' a difficult question.}}
#: {{ux|nl|Ze '''stelde''' het probleem voor aan het team.|She '''put forward''' the problem to the team.}}
#: {{ux|nl|Na het college is er gelegenheid om vragen te '''stellen'''.|There is an opportunity to '''ask''' questions after class.}}
# {{lb|nl|transitive}} to [[suppose]] (commonly as an imperative and followed by a clause beginning with {{m|nl|dat}})
#: {{ux|nl|'''Stel''' dat we naar Mars kunnen reizen.|'''Suppose''' that we can travel to Mars.}}
#: {{ux|nl|'''Stel''' dat ik de loterij win.|'''Suppose''' I win the lottery.}}
# {{lb|nl|reflexive}} to take one's stand
#: {{ux|nl|De soldaten '''stelden''' zich op in formatie.|The soldiers '''took their stand''' in formation.}}
#: {{ux|nl|Ze '''stelde''' zich op tegen het onrecht.|She '''took her stand''' against the injustice.}}
# {{lb|nl|transitive|chemistry}} to [[standardize]] a solution by titration
#: {{ux|nl|De laborant '''stelde''' de oplossing op punt door titratie.|The laboratory assistant '''standardized''' the solution by titration.}}
#: {{ux|nl|We moeten de zoutoplossing '''stellen''' met behulp van titratie.|We need to '''standardize''' the saline solution using titration.}}

