==German==

===Etymology===
{{root|de|ine-pro|*stel-}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|stellen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|stellen}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*stalljan|t=to put, position}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*stel-|t=to place, put, post, stand}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃtɛlən/|[ˈʃtɛ.l̩n]|[-lən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-stellen.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-stellen2.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-stellen.ogg|a=Austria}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} {{causative of|de|stehen}}: to [[put]], [[place]], [[position]] (someone or something) such that it [[stand]]s [[upright]]
#: {{cot|de|setzen|legen}}
#: {{uxi|de|'''Stell''' die Flasche auf den Boden!|'''Put''' the bottle on the floor!}}
## {{lb|de|figuratively|abstractly}} to [[pose]], to [[lodge]]
##: {{ux|de|Die Beklagte '''stellte''' den Antrag, die Klage abzuweisen.|The defendant '''lodged''' the application to reject the claim.}}
##: {{ux|de|Kann ich dir eine Frage '''stellen'''?|Can I '''ask''' you a question?}}
## to [[provide]], to [[afford]], to place at someone's [[disposal]]
##: {{ux|de|Die Schutzbekleidung muss vom Arbeitgeber '''gestellt''' werden.|The protective gear must be '''provided''' by the employer.}}
##: {{ux|de|Aus dem Sicherungsvertrage war die A-Gesellschaft verpflichtet, eine Bürgschaft zu '''stellen'''.|From the surety agreement the A company was obliged to '''provide''' a suretyship.}}
## to [[encounter]] and [[stop]]
##: {{ux|de|Die Hunde haben den Hirsch '''gestellt'''.|The hounds '''stopped''' the stag.}}
##: {{ux|de|Die Polizei stellte den Dieb.|The police '''stopped (and arrested)''' the thief.}}
## to [[set]], [[adjust]]
##: {{syn|de|einstellen}}
##: {{ux|de|Müssen wir am Sonntag wieder die Uhren '''stellen'''?|Do we have to '''adjust''' the clocks again on Sunday?}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[expose]] oneself to, to [[succumb]] to, to come out to [[face]], to [[confront]] {{+obj|de|dat<danger, etc.>}}
#: {{ux|de|Du musst '''dich''' der Gefahr '''stellen'''.|You have to '''face''' the danger.}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Dieb '''stellte sich''' der Polizei.|The thief '''surrendered''' to the police.}}
#* {{quote-song|de|artist=Arische Jugend|title=Brief von der Front|year=2006|album=Sturmabende|track=10|time=2:39–2:49|passage=Wir '''stellen uns''' den Panzern und Granaten,<br>Dem Feinde, der uns gegenüber ficht,<br/>Denn was ist schon das Leben des Soldaten?<br/>Der Tod fürs Volk die Heldenpflicht.|translation=We '''will face''' the tanks and grenades<br/>The enemy who fights in front of us<br/>For what is the life of the soldier<br/>Death for the people is the obligation of a hero}}
# {{senseid|de|pretend}} to [[feign]], to [[simulate]], to [[pretend]]
## {{lb|de|transitive}}
##: {{uxi|de|Es war alles nur '''gestellt!'''|It was all '''fake'''!}}
##: {{uxi|de|Sie hatte ihre Krankheit nur '''gestellt'''.|She merely '''simulated''' her ailment.}}
## {{lb|de|reflexive}} {{+obj|de|adjective/present participle}}
##: {{coi|de|sich tot '''stellen'''|to [[play dead|'''play''' dead]]}}

